WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.507
Before moving into RAG, try to explain the main Transformer ideas without reading definitions.

00:00:06.507 --> 00:00:11.032
What is the difference between a token ID and an embedding vector?

00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:15.032
Why do we need an attention mask when padding is present?

00:00:15.032 --> 00:00:18.547
Where do Q, K, and V come from, and what role does each one play?

00:00:18.547 --> 00:00:26.242
Why can the word bank end with different hidden representations in two sentences?

00:00:26.242 --> 00:00:30.042
How does causal masking change decoder attention?

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:33.097
When would you start with an encoder-only model rather than a decoder-only model?

00:00:33.097 --> 00:00:41.582
What does pretrained mean, and why do most applied projects start from pretrained weights instead of random

00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:43.827
initialization?

00:00:43.827 --> 00:00:48.282
Finally, why would semantic search use a sentence-embedding model rather than a general text-generation model?

00:00:48.282 --> 00:00:56.097
If you can answer these in your own words and connect them to the Python examples,

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:58.855
you have the foundation needed for the next module.
